Package: specshiny
Title: Neuro-Symbolic Specification Engine for Dynamic 'Shiny' UIs
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Marcus", "Harris", , "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Implements a neuro-symbolic architecture that compiles
    natural-language descriptions of statistical and simulation studies into a
    strictly schema-validated intermediate representation (IR) with statistical
    sanity guardrails, dynamically synthesizes context-specific 'bslib' and
    'Shiny' user interfaces with bidirectional synchronization, undo/redo
    history, and visual change diffs, and deterministically compiles validated
    specifications into AST-verified standalone R scripts, 'Quarto' reports,
    and reproducible study bundles without evaluating untrusted language model
    output (supporting offline rule-based parsing as well as 'OpenAI' and
    'Ollama' backends using 'YAML' and 'JSON' serialization).
